  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <h3>Is FinBrio free?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes — the core app is free, including live markets across 46 indices, 23 commodities and
    44 forex pairs, AI signals on strategies S1–S3, the Power Moves scanner, smart-money
    tracking, tariff exposure, the ETF explorer, and the macro dashboard. A single Pro
    subscription unlocks the market-cap treemap, advanced strategies, unlimited alerts and
    analyst notes, AI-powered analysis, and API access.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I manage or cancel a subscription?</h3>
  <p>
    Subscriptions are billed through the Apple App Store or Google Play. Manage or cancel any
    time from your device's subscription settings — on iOS via Settings → your name →
    Subscriptions, and on Android via the Play Store → Subscriptions.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I restore a purchase?</h3>
  <p>
    Open FinBrio, go to your profile, and use "Restore purchases." Your entitlement will
    reactivate on any device signed in to the same app-store account.
  </p>

  <h3>Are the signals financial advice?</h3>
  <p>
    No. FinBrio is an information and analytics tool. Signals, backtests, and briefings are
    for informational purposes only and are not investment advice. Markets involve risk —
    always do your own research.
  </p>

  <h3>Where does the data come from?</h3>
  <p>
    Market data from Yahoo Finance; hedge-fund positioning from the CFTC; the debt clock from
    the US Treasury; tariff data from USTR Section 301 schedules; congressional and insider
    filings from official public disclosures including SEC EDGAR; and country statistics from
    the World Bank.
  </p>

  <h3>How do I delete my account?</h3>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@finbrio.net">support@finbrio.net</a> from your account
    address and we'll remove your account and associated data.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle your data.
  </p>
</Legal>
